  "body": "## Scope\n\nDeep negotiation audit/fix on top of stable `4bf244ef`. This PR is intentionally limited to conversation/negotiation integrity and does not change catalog category/filter selection.\n\n## Confirmed issues fixed\n\n- Explicit Vinted `PENDING` offers could become `EXPIRED` after 48h and disappear from active negotiations even though Vinted still showed them as pending.\n- A read indicator or ordinary seller chat message could trigger a hidden 3h automatic price increase while the previous offer was still formally pending.\n- Three ambiguous checks with missing composer/offer controls could terminalize a conversation as `CONTACT_UNAVAILABLE` without explicit block/contact-disabled evidence.\n- Seller counteroffers could become `REJECTED` when there was no safe automatic next step, even though the seller had made an actionable live price proposal.\n- Vinted status parsing only recognized narrow Polish forms (`Oczekujące/Zaakceptowane/Odrzucone`).\n- A DOM price misread above the original listing price could be treated as a seller counteroffer.\n- First-offer and conversation navigation did not consistently use the shared session-refresh-safe navigator.\n- Non-adaptive negotiation ladders were not required by backend validation to be strictly increasing.\n- Runtime next-step validation did not reject a price <= the current sent offer.\n- A real first offer could succeed on Vinted while redirect/backend persistence failed after the click, leaving the listing outside `NEGOTIATING`.\n\n## Behavior after this PR\n\n- While Vinted explicitly says the latest own offer is pending, the listing stays `NEGOTIATING` indefinitely. Read/message/time alone never raises the price and never terminalizes it.\n- Only formal rejection/counteroffer policies advance the ladder. Their configured waits remain authoritative.\n- Seller counteroffer with no safe automatic next step becomes `ACTION_REQUIRED`, not `REJECTED`.\n- Only explicit block/contact-disabled evidence may set `CONTACT_UNAVAILABLE`; ambiguous missing controls remain active and retry later.\n- Status variants are matched by stable stems; impossible seller prices fail closed as UNKNOWN.\n- First-offer ambiguous post-submit recovery is allowed only with strong item-bound conversation URL evidence plus the exact expected latest own-offer price; it never clicks submit again.\n- Existing `EXPIRED` / `CONTACT_UNAVAILABLE` rows with valid conversation identity are re-opened once by V41 so the real Vinted conversation can be inspected again.\n- Offer ladders must increase in every pricing mode, with an additional runtime check before a next-step submit.\n\n## Known safety choice\n\nConfigured chat messages remain best-effort after a confirmed price offer. If a message send is ambiguous, Flipbot does not retry it automatically because doing so could duplicate the message. Price offers remain guarded separately by persistent action guards/quota idempotency.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdds/extends regression coverage for:\n- pending retention after elapsed time/read/seller chat,\n- accepted/rejected/pending Vinted status variants,\n- impossible seller counteroffer evidence,\n- last-step seller counteroffer -> ACTION_REQUIRED,\n- increasing ladders in non-adaptive mode,\n- refresh-safe arbitrary Vinted navigation.\n",
